{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.findings.f28.control",
    "description": "F28's CONTROL, and it is MEANT TO PASS. It is the workaround for the finding in the file beside it: a recurrence whose predecessor is named by a data column, re-expressed as a BOUNDED CONTRACTED LAG.\n\nThe contracted index `a` runs over the lag's whole observed range and the body selects the one term whose lag matches the data column, `ifelse(lag[k] == a, ...)`, summing the rest as the additive identity. That is esm-spec 4.3.1.1's straddling idiom and docs/esm-conventions.md 19.2's rule that the contracted index IS the lag -- the same shape `agedist.f`'s fold uses, applied to a predecessor that a column names rather than the slot number.\n\nTwo costs, and they are why the finding is recorded rather than the workaround simply being used. It evaluates `max lag` terms per cell where the direct spelling would evaluate one, so a chain whose lags are mostly 1 pays for the worst case at every cell. And the range `[1, 7]` is a METAPARAMETER expression that has to be right: it is read off the DATA (the largest `tripID - priorTripID` in the snapshot's 26,300 chained trips), so it is a fact about a capture and not about the model, and a lag beyond it would silently contribute nothing rather than raise. That second cost is the one worth pausing on -- an under-sized range is this repository's characteristic failure, a plausible number in place of an answer.\n\nIt is excluded from run-tests.sh's tripwire loop by name, for the same reason F18's and F24b's controls are: a file that is meant to pass would be read by that loop as a defect that has been fixed.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "finding",
      "recurrence"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "f28_rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "F28Control": {
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-12
      },
      "variables": {
        "f28_lag": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "f28_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many rows back this row's predecessor is. Row 1 has none. The shape of `SampleVehicleTrip.tripID - priorTripID` in miniature: mostly 1, sometimes more."
        },
        "f28_value": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "f28_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`v[k] = 2 * v[k - lag[k]]`, spelled as a contracted lag: one term per candidate lag, all but the matching one contributing 0."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "f28_lag",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": [
              0,
              1,
              1,
              2,
              1,
              3
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The workaround. `a` is contracted over the lag's bounded range and the equality against the data column selects the single term that is not the additive identity; the no-predecessor case is carried on the a = 1 slot so that it is emitted exactly once rather than max-lag times.",
          "lhs": "f28_value",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
              "k"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "k": {
                "from": "f28_rows"
              },
              "a": [
                1,
                7
              ]
            },
            "reduce": "+",
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "<=",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "f28_lag",
                        "k"
                      ]
                    },
                    0
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "ifelse",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "==",
                      "args": [
                        "a",
                        1
                      ]
                    },
                    1.0,
                    0.0
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "ifelse",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "==",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "f28_lag",
                            "k"
                          ]
                        },
                        "a"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        2.0,
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "f28_value",
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "k",
                                "a"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    0.0
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_contracted_lag_reproduces_the_data_named_chain",
          "description": "The same six answers the finding's repro asks for, obtained through the contracted-lag spelling. Row 4 reads row 2 and row 6 reads row 3, so the chain really is following the data column and not a constant offset -- with a constant lag of 1 the answers would be [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32] and five of these six assertions would fail.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "f28_value",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "f28_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "f28_value",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2.0,
              "coords": {
                "f28_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "f28_value",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 4.0,
              "coords": {
                "f28_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "f28_value",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 4.0,
              "coords": {
                "f28_rows": 4
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "f28_value",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "f28_rows": 5
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "f28_value",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "f28_rows": 6
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
